{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ConfinementCategorical","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ConfinementCategorical","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.int_factors_through_centre_of_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.int_factors_through_centre_of_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L98-L110","doc":"**Repaired form of the removed axiom.** If the trace is invariant under\nthe centre projection, `intA (π_Z a) = intA a`, then it factors through\nthe centre: `intA = μ ∘ π_Z` with `μ := intA|_Z`.\n\nThe content is entirely in the hypothesis. For `H_n(q)` it is the\nstatement that the Markov trace sees only Wedderburn residues, which is\nstill to be proved for the concrete `π_Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.not_int_factors_through_centre_unconstrained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.not_int_factors_through_centre_unconstrained","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L88-L96","doc":"**The former axiom is false.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.zeroCentreInstance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.zeroCentreInstance","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L78-L86","doc":"An instance on `ℤ` with zero centre submodule and zero projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.confinement_survives_only_centre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.confinement_survives_only_centre","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L49-L61","doc":"**Theorem (clause 1 — survival).**\nOnly `E_∞^{0,0} = Z(A)` survives the spectral sequence: the centre\nprojection `π_Z` acts as the identity on the surviving centre `Z(A)`\n(every central element is its own residue, all non-central\ncomponents are projected away). Derived from `piZ_fixes_centre`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.piZ_fixes_centre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.piZ_fixes_centre","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L46-L46","doc":"`π_Z` is a genuine projection onto the centre: it restricts to the\nidentity on central elements (`a ∈ Z ⇒ π_Z a = a`). This is the\nalgebraic shadow of \"only `E_∞^{0,0} = Z(A)` survives\": the\nprojection fixes exactly the surviving centre and kills the rest.\n(Semisimplicity / Whitehead-lemma cohomology vanishing in positive\ndegree is what makes `π_Z` well-defined as a centre projection.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.piZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.piZ","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Centre projection (Wedderburn): `π_Z(a) = Σ_λ e_λ · a · e_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.Z","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Centre as an explicit sub-`R`-module (Wedderburn). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Cyclicity: the integral vanishes on commutators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.intA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.intA","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Frobenius integral: the Markov trace as `R`-linear map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike.mk","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleFrobeniusHeckeLike","kind":"class","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/confinement-categorical.lean#L28-L46","doc":"A semisimple Frobenius algebra `A` over a commutative ring `R`,\nabstracting `H_n(R, q)` for generic `q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}